    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-981-96-4967-9_50",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-981-96-4967-9_50",
      "title": "Spacecraft On-Orbit Servicing Summary of Mission Planning Research",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Yabo Hao, Dandan Wang, ... Xue Bai"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "The number of spacecrafts performing on-orbit missions has increased sharply because of the rapid development of the space industry, and the types of missions are diverse. In order to save fuel and time as much as possible during on-orbit service, the research on spacecraft service-oriented mission planning has become an international hot spot. This paper first introduces the connotation of on-orbit service mission planning, and then introduces the solution algorithm. In general, the study of spacecraft on-orbit service mission planning can provide theoretical support for engineering practice, and provide technical support for military observation, navigation planning, disaster prevention and control, land mapping and many other aspects.",
